[2026-07-22] CODING LOG
- tools/extract_sectors.py: extracts sector dots from IMG_7078.gif.
  Pass 1 (bright + near-neutral) -> 1921 dots; pass 2 (bright + saturated, for
  dots under faction-color overlays) -> +102, total 2023. Filters: erosion x3
  kills thin lines/text; blob area 8-400 px, aspect <= 2.2, bbox fill >= 0.45
  keep only round dot blobs. Output data/sectors_raw.json in galaxy coords
  (core at origin, half-extent 150 to match old star-map.py macro view).
- stellarforge.py: core library.
  * Deterministic seeding: sha256("TRF-GALAXY-V1/...path") -> 64-bit seeds for
    numpy default_rng. Python's hash() avoided (salted per process).
  * Galaxy: loads catalog, stable sector ordering (sort by angle,radius), derives
    per-sector r, local density (kNN), age (11.5 -> 5 Gyr inside-out + noise),
    [Fe/H] (+0.35 -> -0.55 gradient + noise), young_frac (arm density driven),
    nebula flags (top-SFR, greedy min-separation), procedural syllable names,
    hyperlane network (MST over kNN graph + short local links).
  * generate_sector_stars(): 10,000 stars/sector. Positions via 8x8 boxel grid
    with lognormal weights + gaussian edge softening (Stellar Forge boxels,
    scaled down). Masses from Kroupa IMF (inverse-CDF, broken power law 1.3/2.3
    at 0.5 Msun). Ages: sector-old population + young_frac recent component.
    Evolution vs MS lifetime 10*M^-2.5 Gyr: giants (0.85-1.0 t_ms), WD (<8 Msun),
    NS (8-25), BH (>25). Flags: habitable (FGK 2%, M 0.4%, x metallicity boost),
    resource_rich (~3% x metallicity), exotic (remnants + 0.1%).
  * generate_system(): on-demand deterministic system from (sector, star index):
    multiplicity by class, planet count Poisson(4 x metallicity), geometric
    orbit spacing, HZ at sqrt(L) AU, types by insolation, gas giants suppressed
    around low-mass hosts, habitable flag honored (guaranteed HZ terrestrial).
  BUGFIX: Kroupa continuity constant was inverted (0.5^-1 instead of 0.5^1),
  made massive stars 4x too common. Caught via class-mix smoke test.
- starmap2.py: UI, feature parity with star-map.py (WASD pan, scroll zoom,
  pickable sectors, nebulae, core black hole + desolate core view, sector view
  with Star Class / Habitable / Resource Rich / Exotic radio filters, back
  buttons) plus new: deterministic revisits, sector metadata in title, and a
  system view (click any star: orbits, HZ ring, planet list).
- Post-research-brief parameter alignment: BH threshold 20->25 Msun (NS:BH ~2:1),
  planet lambda 2.5->4.0, habitable flag rates raised to 0.02/0.004.

[2026-07-22] PERFORMANCE PASS (galaxy view lag)
- Profiled per-layer draw cost (Agg): full frame 104.5 ms. Haze scatter (6,069
  s=900 alpha markers) 66.7 ms, nebulae (378 individual Circle patches) 21.9 ms,
  lanes 7.5 ms, dots 4.4 ms. Cause: matplotlib re-rasterizes every artist on
  every pan/zoom; the soft glow layers blend ~9M px of alpha per frame.
- Fix 1: baked haze + nebulae into one cached 1000px RGBA image (imshow,
  _galaxy_background). Bake vectorized (haze as one scatter): 0.32 s one-time.
- Found matplotlib 3.5's image path is OUTPUT-bound: even an 8px source costs
  ~45 ms/frame (viewport-sized resample each draw), so smaller bakes / nearest
  interpolation / opaque RGB all plateau around 37-52 ms.
- Fix 2: defer_artist_during_interaction() - background hidden during
  scroll/WASD events, restored by a 200 ms single-shot canvas timer after
  interaction stops. add_scroll_zoom/add_wasd_pan grew an on_interact hook;
  clear_fig stops the timer on view change.
- Result: interaction frames 105 -> 14.1 ms (~70 fps); idle full-quality frame
  46 ms (drawn once); first bake 0.32 s; re-render verders visually identical.

[2026-07-22] 80K STARS + SMOOTH PAN + EDGE-PLACEMENT PASS
- Spec change: sectors now average ~80,000 stars (was fixed 10,000).
  sector_star_count(): deterministic per-sector N(80k x density modifier,
  7k sd) clamped 55k-110k; all-sector mean 78.6k. Marker sizes retuned for
  the 8x denser field (back to old star-map.py scale).
- WASD panning rebuilt: was one 10% jump per key_press (OS auto-repeat ->
  jumpy). Now key press/release maintain a held-key set and a repeating 33 ms
  canvas timer glides the view 2.5%/tick while keys are held; diagonal works;
  clear_fig stops the timer and disconnects the release handler.
- Star placement fix: boxel jitter was np.clip'd to [0,100], piling stars
  into visible lines along the sector border (worse at 80k). Jitter is now
  reflected back inside, and boxel weights get a gaussian radial envelope
  (sigma 38) so density thins toward sector edges - star field, not filled
  square. Sector axes padded to (-3,103) so nothing sits on the frame.
- Sector view perf at ~90k stars (183 ms/frame raster cost, antialiasing
  irrelevant): defer_artist_during_interaction gained a `placeholder` arg -
  during zoom a 1/6-decimated preview scatter (34 ms/frame) stands in for the
  full field, which restores on idle. Radio overlay modes update the preview's
  colors/sizes too so the stand-in matches the active mode.

[2026-07-22] FILTER PICKING FIX
- Bug: filter modes only dimmed non-matching stars; all ~80k stars stayed
  pickable and on_pick took evt.ind[0] (lowest index near the click), so
  clicking a highlighted dot usually opened some unrelated background star.
- Fix 1: filter modes now swap the full-field scatter for a `filt` scatter
  containing ONLY the matching stars (set_offsets of the flagged subset);
  filtered-out stars are removed entirely, not dimmed. state['filt_idx'] maps
  subset positions back to true star indices. Title shows "X of N stars".
- Fix 2: picks resolve via nearest_to_click() - among the pick candidates,
  choose the star closest to the actual click coordinates (both in full-field
  and filtered modes).
- Interaction deferral (preview swap) now only runs in Star Class mode; the
  filtered subsets are small enough to draw directly every frame.
